# One name per path.  mkv10 reads this when it lays the tapes down.
#
# The six tapes are case-sensitive and this tree has to survive a case-INSENSITIVE
# checkout, so wherever two tape paths differ only in case exactly one of them can
# keep its name.  RULE 0 DECIDES WHICH: the survivor is whatever the directory's own
# build file names -- NOT whatever is lowercase.
#
# Lowercase-wins was the earlier rule and it is wrong twice over.  ostdio's
# olibcmkfile:123 is `doprnt.o: stdio/doprnt.S', so the build reads the capitalised
# file and lowercase-wins renamed the one thing that had to keep its name;
# cfront/libstring's makefile names String.h seven times and string.h never.  A
# rename this project's own tooling performed then had to be undone by a block in
# `patch', on the machine, at build time.
#
# TWO RECORD TYPES, and both are relative to the tape's own spelling:
#
#   NAME <tape path> <our path>    extract it under our name instead
#   DROP <tape path>               do not extract it at all
#
# Nothing else is a decision.  A tape path absent from this file is extracted
# under its own name, which is almost all of them.
#
# DROP is used for three things and nothing else: a *.o or *.O, which is build
# output the tape happened to ship (ipnxclean's rule, and 91 of them collided);
# a file the build REGENERATES from the sibling it collides with -- compress's
# makefile:10-11 is `USERMEM:' / `sh usermem > USERMEM', and both Version.c come
# from `./version > Version.c'; and a redundant duplicate -- six zero-byte
# ipc/bin merge artefacts, sail's hard link, and libstring/string.h which no
# source includes and no build file names.
#
# THE 34 TROFF FONT DESCRIPTIONS CANNOT BE RENAMED and are the reason this file
# has to be read at install time too, not only here.  devpost/Hb opens
# `name Hb / fontname Helvetica-Narrow-Bold' and devpost/HB opens `name HB /
# fontname Helvetica-Bold': the FILENAME IS THE FONT'S IDENTITY and troff
# resolves a .ft request to a file of that name at run time.  Renaming one does
# not break a build -- it breaks documents, silently, by falling back to a
# different weight.  So they carry a distinct name here and the build must
# install them under the tape's.

